[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3705242537","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114503#issuecomment-3705242537","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114503","id":3705242537,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7c2YOp","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-02T12:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T12:37:05Z","body":"> ### Steps to reproduce\n> \n> deleting the sprite while the UV preview dialog is open\n\nTo be clear, how exactly do you do that?\n\nI could indeed reproduce the crash by:\n1. Enqueue the sprite deletion on a timer's `timeout`, from `@tool` script.\n2. Before the `timeout`, open the dialog for that sprite.\n3. `timeout` emits, sprite is deleted while the dialog is still opened.\n4. E.g. trying to zoom in the dialog make the editor crash.\n\nBut AFAICT from the UI itself you shouldn't be able to delete the edited Sprite2D while the \"UV preview dialog\" is opened, the dialog should be in exclusive mode. Is it maybe not the case on iOS (I've tested on Windows) or something like that?","author_associat